TYPES.md §3.1, GRAMMAR.md §7.1 (DECISIONS 380): a selected package importing a later tier is E2007 in the selected package; the unplaced c, not selected, is still E1018 (ADR-0021 §4 point 14).
-- check-only --
-- select --
a
-- project.canon --
project acme {
  canon: "0.1"
  tiers {
    low: [a]
    high: [b]
  }
}
-- a/a.canon --
package a

import b
-- b/b.canon --
package b
-- c/c.canon --
package c
-- findings.txt --
error[E2007]  a/a.canon:3:8
  a (tier low) cannot import b (tier high): a package imports only from its own tier and the tiers listed before it in project.canon

error[E1018]  project.canon:3:3
  tiers: no tier places package c; list it, or a package path above it, in a tier

2 errors, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
